\cf2 \cb5 Context Awareness\cb1 \cell 
\pard\intbl\itap1\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Use a "Transaction ID." Each prompt sent to Kimi 2.5 should include the Version ID of the graph it\'92s currently looking at.\cb1 \cell \lastrow\row
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf6 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 3. Refining the "Main Network" (The Router)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Since you want the Main Network to remain "light," don't store actual data there. Think of it as a Semantic Table of Contents.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Logic: When you mention a new topic (e.g., "Let's talk about Quantum Physics"), the AI checks the Main Network.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Action: If "Quantum Physics" isn't there, the AI creates a temporary local graph.\cb1 \
\ls7\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Integration: Only once that conversation concludes (or reaches a milestone) does the async process "promote" that local graph into a official sub-network and update the Main Network's "Map" to include it.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 4. Questions to Finalize the Idea:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
State Management: Since you are a Laravel developer, are you planning to use Livewire or a similar stateful frontend to manage the "Active Buffer," or are you relying entirely on the LLM's API history?\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Extraction Trigger: Should the "Update" happen after every message (high resource cost) or after a "Natural Pause" in the conversation (e.g., 30 seconds of inactivity)?\cb1 \
\ls8\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Conflict Resolution: If the "New Data" being logged contradicts an old node in the graph, does the AI have permission to "delete" or "archive" the old node automatically?\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Note on Kimi 2.5: Since you mentioned Kimi 2.5, keep in mind its Thinking Mode. You can actually ask the model in its "hidden" reasoning phase to decide if a piece of information is "Graph-Worthy" or just "Chatter." This saves you from cluttering your networks with "Hello" and "How are you."\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
