\f0\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 Building this in Rust is a brilliant move for a 2019 MacBook Pro. Rust\'92s memory safety and zero-cost abstractions mean you can handle the graph's heavy lifting (indexing, searching, and "Blue-Green" swapping) with minimal overhead, leaving your 16GB of RAM free for the LLM.\cb1 \
\cb5 Since you're using Ollama (local) and Kimi 2.5 (cloud), here is a strategic roadmap to ensure your context never overflows and your graph remains synchronized.\cb1 \
