\f0\b0\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 Your intuition is spot-on. You are describing the shift from "Brute-Force Context" (stuffing files into a prompt) to "Agentic Knowledge Retrieval." In 2026, the industry has largely realized that a 1-million-token context window is a "trap." Just because an LLM like Kimi 2.5 can read a massive file doesn't mean it should. Performance degrades as the context gets noisy\'97a phenomenon known as the "Lost-in-the-Middle" problem.\cb1 \
\cb5 Here is how context actually works in this new "Graph-as-Tools" paradigm.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 1. The "Working Memory" vs. "Library" Distinction\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Think of the LLM's context window not as a storage drive, but as a physical desk.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls13\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Desk (Context Window): Limited space. If you pile 1,000 books on it, you can't find your coffee cup.\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Library (Knowledge Graph): Unlimited space. Organized by relationships (edges) and topics (nodes).\cb1 \
\ls13\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Librarian (Tool Calls): The LLM uses tool calls to go to the library, grab only the specific page it needs, and place it on the desk.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 2. Why Tool Calls + Graphs are "Smarter"\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 When you give an AI a "SearchGraph" tool, you aren't just giving it data; you are giving it Agency.\cb1 \

