\cf2 \cb5 5. Technical Implementation in Rust (The "Librarian" Pattern)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 In your Rust code, you can define a trait for your modes:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf4 \cb9 Rust\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf10 \cb9 trait\cf13  AgentMode\cf4  \{\
    \cf10 fn\cf4  \cf13 can_write\cf4 (&\cf10 self\cf4 ) -> \cf14 bool\cf4 ;\
    \cf10 fn\cf4  \cf13 get_system_prompt\cf4 (&\cf10 self\cf4 ) -> \cf14 String\cf4 ;\
\}\
\
\cf10 struct\cf13  Reviewer\cf4 ;\
\cf10 impl\cf4  AgentMode \cf10 for\cf4  Reviewer \{\
    \cf10 fn\cf4  \cf13 can_write\cf4 (&\cf10 self\cf4 ) -> \cf14 bool\cf4  \{ \cf15 true\cf4  \}\
    \cf10 fn\cf4  \cf13 get_system_prompt\cf4 (&\cf10 self\cf4 ) -> \cf14 String\cf4  \{ \
        \cf12 "Extract deductions, check for conflicts, and update weights..."\cf4 .to_string() \
    \}\
\}\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 By enforcing 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 can_write == false
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  for the Researcher and Actor at the code level, you ensure that even if the LLM "tries" to call a 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 save_node
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  tool during those phases, the Rust backend will reject the request.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Summary of the "3-Man" Strategy:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls30\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Researcher: "What do we know about this?" (Read: Gold + Drafts)\cb1 \
\ls30\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Actor: "Here is the answer based on what we know." (Read: Gold + Drafts)\cb1 \
\ls30\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Reviewer (Async): "What did we learn? Does it conflict? Update the scores." (Read: All | Write: All)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 This setup is the "Gold Standard" for local LLM memory. It prevents the 20GB bloat because the Reviewer is actively distilling and deleting low-confidence or redundant noise.\cb1 \
