\ls34\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Researcher/Actor Tool Registry:\
\ls34\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
In Rust, you\'92ll define a 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 Registry
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  that only exposes 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 query_graph()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  to the Researcher and Actor.\cb1 \
\ls34\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Reviewer Tool Registry:\
\ls34\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Reviewer\'92s registry includes 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 upsert_node()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 , 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 delete_node()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 , and 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 adjust_weight()
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 .\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Why this connects so well:\
Because you are using Rust, the 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 data/subgraphs/
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  can be stored as tiny, high-performance binary files (like 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 .db
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  or 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 .surreal
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 ). When the Actor mentions "Laravel," the Researcher only "mounts" the 
\fs28 \cf4 \cb3 laravel.db
\fs32 \cf2 \cb5  file. This keeps your RAM usage extremely low, even as your total knowledge grows to 100GB+.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Summary of Benefits:\cb1 \
