\fs44 \cf2 \cb5 Project Specification: Cognitive Graph Memory Engine (CGME)\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb5 1. Project Overview\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 A high-performance, Rust-based Dynamic Hierarchical Knowledge Graph (HKG) designed for persistent AI memory. The engine operates as a standalone library and CLI "Skill" that orchestrates LLMs to extract, verify, and store deductions rather than raw conversational transcripts.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb5 2. Core Architecture: The "3-Man" Operation\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 The system splits labor into three distinct asynchronous roles to ensure data integrity and prevent context bloat:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Researcher (Read-Only): * Scans user input and queries the Main Network (The Map).\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl1\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Retrieves relevant "Gold" and "Draft" nodes from sub-graphs.\cb1 \
\ls49\ilvl1\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Prepares the context packet for the Actor.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Actor (Read-Only):\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl1\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Generates the user-facing response using retrieved context + short-term history.\cb1 \
\ls49\ilvl1\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Prioritizes current conversation flow over stale graph data.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Reviewer (Read/Write - Async):\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls49\ilvl1\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Performs Deduction-Based Synthesis (extracts facts, not fluff).\cb1 \
\ls49\ilvl1\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Calculates Confidence Scores based on repetition and explicit confirmation.\cb1 \
\ls49\ilvl1\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Manages conflict resolution (e.g., updating outdated tech stack info).\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb5 3. Data Strategy & Storage\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs32 \cf2 \cb5 Hierarchical Structure\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls50\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Main Network (The Router): A lightweight index mapping semantic topics to specific sub-graph UUIDs.\cb1 \
\ls50\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Sub-Graphs: Topic-specific clusters (e.g., "Laravel Development," "Personal History") to keep the LLM's working memory lean.\cb1 \
\ls50\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Tiered Access: * Gold Tier: Verified facts (
\fs38\fsmilli19360 Score>80
\fs32 ).\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls50\ilvl1\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Draft Tier: Recent deductions (
\fs38\fsmilli19360 Score<50
\fs32 ) awaiting reinforcement.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 Blue-Green Deployment Logic\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \cb5 To allow real-time updates without blocking the conversation:\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls51\ilvl0\cf2 \cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The active graph (Blue) serves the Researcher and Actor.\cb1 \
\ls51\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The Reviewer writes updates to a twin instance (Green).\cb1 \
\ls51\ilvl0\cb5 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Once the Reviewer validates the new state, the system performs an Atomic Swap in Rust, making Green the new Blue.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs40 \cf2 \cb5 4. Technical Stack\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa200\partightenfactor0
\ls52\ilvl0
