\cb9 # uncver-kg 
\f5 \uc0\u55357 \u56589 
\f0 \
\
**uncver-kg** (Uncover Knowledge Graph) is a lightweight, high-performance Rust library and CLI tool designed to give AI a persistent, evolving memory. \
\
Instead of just storing chat logs, \cf12 `uncver-kg`\cf4  uses a **3-Agent Orchestration** to distill conversations into a structured **Hierarchical Knowledge Graph**, ensuring your LLM remembers deductions, not just noise.\
\
## 
\f5 \uc0\u55357 \u56960 
\f0  Key Features\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf16 -\cf4  **Library & CLI:** Use it as a Rust crate in your apps or as a standalone \cf12 `uncverkg`\cf4  command.\
\cf16 -\cf4  **Deduction-Based Memory:** Only saves verified facts and logical deductions.\
\cf16 -\cf4  **Oxigraph Engine:** Uses a native Rust graph store for lightning-fast local performance.\
\cf16 -\cf4  **Gemma 4 Optimized:** Built to leverage the "Thinking" process of local models via Ollama.\
\cf16 -\cf4  **Zero-Bloat JSON:** Config and stats are stored in plain JSON for easy inspection.\
\
## 
\f5 \uc0\u55357 \u57056 
\f0  Quick Start\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf12 ```bash\
# Install via Cargo (coming soon) or build from source\
cargo build --release\
\
# Initialize config\
uncverkg init\
\
# Start a session with Gemma 4\
uncverkg prompt "David is migrating the Bethel App to AWS next Tuesday."\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
