# Architecture: uncver-kg\
\
## 1. The Storage Stack\
We use a hybrid storage approach to balance performance, human-readability, and historical tracking:\
\
* **Knowledge Graph (Oxigraph):** Stores the actual triples (Subject-Predicate-Object). We use "Named Graphs" to separate **Gold** (verified) and **Draft** (unverified) data.\
* **Statistics (SQLite/Sled):** A relational or KV database used to store periodic snapshots of the graph state. This allows for time-series analysis of "learning" progress.\
* **Configuration (JSON):** A simple `config.json` for user settings (API keys, model names, confidence thresholds).\
\
## 2. The 3-Man Operation (Agentic Logic)\
| Agent | Role | Execution |\
| :--- | :--- | :--- |\
| **Researcher** | Retrieves context using semantic search + graph traversal. | Read-Only |\
| **Actor** | Processes the user prompt using retrieved context. | Read-Only |\
| **Reviewer** | Analyzes the exchange, extracts deductions, and commits updates. | Read/Write |\
\
## 3. Atomic Updates (Blue-Green)\
To ensure the Actor always has a stable view of the world:\
1. The **Reviewer** prepares updates in a background transaction.\
2. Once validated, the **Storage Engine** performs an atomic swap of the active graph pointer.\
3. The old version is archived or pruned based on the retention policy.\
